-- title:
--   Λ-torsor grading of a Hopf algebra block
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an exponent $k$, and a finite abelian group $\Lambda$ (with decidable equality) killed by $q^k$, i.e. $(q^k)\cdot g=0$ for all $g\in\Lambda$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$, and let $O$ be a commutative domain equipped with an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra structure whose structure map is injective (faithful scalar action) and sends every element of $O$ into $A$; assume $O$ is a discrete valuation ring in which $q$ is irreducible. Let $HO$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $O$ that is module-finite and flat over $O$ and has cocommutative comultiplication, let $p_0\colon HO\to O[\Lambda]=$ `MonoidAlgebra O (Multiplicative Λ)` be a surjective bialgebra map, and let $e\in HO$ be an idempotent such that exactly $\#\Lambda$ of the $O$-algebra maps $\psi\colon HO\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (taken in the convolution type synonym `WithConv`) satisfy $\psi(e)=1$. For $j\in\Lambda$ write $L_j$ for [`HopfAlgebra.TorsorGrading.blockPiece Λ p₀ e j`](def/HopfAlgebra_TorsorGrading.html#L60), the $O$-submodule of those $t\in HO$ with $te=t$ whose $\Lambda$-components — obtained by applying comultiplication, then $p_0$ on the left tensor factor, and reading off coefficients as an element of $\mathrm{Multiplicative}\,\Lambda\to_{0}HO$ — equal the single Finsupp supported at $j$ with value $t$. The conclusion is the conjunction of five assertions: $L_0=O\cdot e$; each $L_j$ is the $O$-span of a single element of $HO$; for all $i,j$, $L_{i+j}$ is contained in the $O$-span of the set of products $xy$ with $x\in L_i$, $y\in L_j$; for all $i,j$, $x\in L_i$ and $y\in L_j$ imply $xy\in L_{i+j}$; and every $x\in HO$ with $xe=x$ lies in $\bigsqcup_{j\in\Lambda}L_j$, the supremum of the submodules $L_j$.
--
--   This is the torsor statement for the block $\operatorname{Spec}(HO\,e)$ cut out by the idempotent $e$: the displayed conditions say that the block is graded by $\Lambda$ into cyclic pieces which multiply according to the group law, with the degree-$0$ piece generated by $e$, which is the algebraic form of the assertion that the block is a torsor under the multiplicative-type group $\operatorname{Spec} O[\Lambda]$. It is used by [`KummerO.exists_units_of_block`](thm.html#KummerO.exists_units_of_block), where the rank-one generators $t_j$ supply the Kummer-theoretic units attached to a finite flat group scheme of multiplicative type.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_blockPieces_torsor_core.lean

